REUSED SOFTWARE

This project uses Lean 4 and mathlib, each licensed under Apache License 2.0.
https://github.com/leanprover/lean4
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4

Generic structure decomposition uses Lean's structure metadata and checked
projection-building APIs. It does not copy an upstream diagram implementation.
The restricted-map view also uses mathlib's PartialEquiv and
OpenPartialHomeomorph definitions at the same pinned revision.
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/8f9d9cff6bd728b17a24e163c9402775d9e6a365/Mathlib/Logic/Equiv/PartialEquiv.lean
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/8f9d9cff6bd728b17a24e163c9402775d9e6a365/Mathlib/Topology/OpenPartialHomeomorph/Defs.lean

The graph vocabulary imports mathlib's simple-graph, coloring, and graph-map definitions
from revision 8f9d9cff6bd728b17a24e163c9402775d9e6a365. These mathematical
constructors are actual dependencies used by the semantic recognizers.
The coloring module credits Arthur Paulino and Kyle Miller; upstream copyright,
license notices, and contributor attribution remain with the dependency sources.
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/8f9d9cff6bd728b17a24e163c9402775d9e6a365/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Coloring.lean
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/8f9d9cff6bd728b17a24e163c9402775d9e6a365/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Maps.lean

