REVIEWED DESIGN REFERENCES

Grant Sanderson's 3Blue1Brown lessons and Manim/ManimGL examples informed ordered
constructions, persistent visual identity, and guided attention.
https://github.com/3b1b/manim
https://www.3blue1brown.com/

Penrose's examples and separation of mathematical vocabulary, relationships,
and visual style informed the semantic-document and renderer boundaries.
https://penrose.cs.cmu.edu/examples
https://penrose.cs.cmu.edu/docs/ref

These are credited sources of design inspiration. No Manim or Penrose code,
scene assets, video assets, or styles were copied or vendored; neither runtime
is included. No third-party diagram implementation is vendored into this repository.
The graph-constraint figures use local SVG and add no graph-layout dependency.
See docs/visual-method.md and docs/graph-iteration.md for the specific application
of these ideas and the distinction between inspiration and software reuse.
